      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Bug / Alignment:** `__##name##_end` and `__##name##_start` are not guaranteed to be 4-byte aligned here. \n\nBecause the zero-fill loop in `init.S` uses a 32-bit store instruction (`strlt r0, [r1], #4`), it expects the start and end addresses to be 4-byte aligned. If the objects placed in this region have a total size that is not a multiple of 4, `__##name##_end` will be unaligned. The loop will then write past the end of the defined objects, potentially corrupting adjacent memory, and unaligned start addresses could trigger hardware alignment faults.\n\n**Remediation:**\nAdd `. \u003d ALIGN(4);` before the start and end symbols to ensure word alignment:\n```assembly\n\t.name(NOLOAD) : { \\\n\t\t. \u003d ALIGN(4); \\\n\t\t__##name##_start \u003d .; \\\n\t\tKEEP(*(SORT(.name.keep.*))) \\\n\t\t*(SORT(.name.*)) \\\n\t\t. \u003d ALIGN(4); \\\n\t\t__##name##_end \u003d .; \\\n\t} \u003e name\n```\n(Apply the same fix to `REGION_LOAD` below).",
